DING GTK 4: reuse desktop windows on margin updates and fix Wayland scaling.

1. Skip premature _updateDesktop() before initial desktopGeometry arrives and
   replace trySpawn(['nautilus', '--version']) with GLib.find_program_in_path,
   avoiding cancelled startup directory enumeration (+500ms retry sleep) and a
   duplicate nautilus process spawn at boot.
2. Resize existing Gtk.ApplicationWindow grids in-place when monitor topology is
   unchanged (e.g. dash-to-panel workarea updates or resolution changes) instead
   of destroying all windows and re-reading ~/Desktop from disk.
3. Keep _size_divisor = 1 on Wayland (Meta.is_stage_views_scaled()), preventing
   double-division of logical monitor dimensions at 200% scale (upstream #368),
   and fix the y-axis typo in DesktopGrid.getDistance().

Upstream component: https://gitlab.com/rastersoft/desktop-icons-ng

